2	//!
3	//! A lazy revision parses and indexes every file, as a cold one does, and stops: no dependency is loaded and no
4	//! component resolved. `Revision::lazy_component` resolves one component when asked, loads only the dependency names
5	//! its resolution reached, and memoizes the result. The memo follows the same dependency tracking watch mode uses
6	//! (`Resolved::affected_by`), so an edit drops exactly the entries it can change.
